+# The FILE rung carries the same untrackedness requirement as .vibe/domains,
+# plus an explicit symlink test on both the file and the .vibe directory
+# itself. Why stricter here than for a profile name: the agent choice decides
+# which runtime's guard chain has to hold, so a committed .vibe/agent would
+# let a pull request choose the lead runtime of every container that clones
+# the repo, and a symlink would let a path outside the project (or outside
+# the work tree git can vouch for) do the same. Every rejection prints ONE
+# `⚠ .vibe/agent ignored: <reason>` line and falls through to the next rung —
+# never fails the launch, and never silently.
+_agent_resolve() {
